{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeeC2qmFmPxXRgK9QDGWi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Waiting for the full-suite run at the final tip. Meanwhile, a summary of where WI-572 round 4 stands:\n\n**All five findings addressed, in three commits plus two follow-ups:**\n\n| Finding | Answer |\n|---|---|\n| MAJOR 1 — brief's population is repo-wide | `Adjudicates` column carries the mint's row-id set; `yours = drafted and rid in scope and _loop_approves(...)`. Measured in-situ: 4 chains/11 rows/3 registries → 1 chain/1 row/1 registry. |\n| MAJOR 2 — smoke red at the tip | `read_specs` walks through `spec_paths` (the read side's own primitive). Smoke went `1 failed, 1455 passed` → **1461 passed, 0 failed**. |\n| MINOR 3 — refusal says \"wrote\" for deletions | `--name-status`, worded from the letter. |\n| MINOR 4 — IF-091 declares a record that never crosses | Clause dropped; the same false claim in the docstring corrected (both halves — `intake` never called it either). |\n| MINOR 5 — docstring contradicts itself | Mirror stated as \"exempted set MINUS the de-approvals\", in all four places that quoted it. |\n\nTwo things the repair uncovered that I did **not** paper over:\n- `live_csv`'s catch-all `ConvertError` skip had kept **four** `test_wi_convert.py` guards dark since WI-504 split the folder home. The skip now fires only on `drained-stop`; the guards measure the registry as the union of both spec roots.\n- `kitlib.registry.WI_COLUMNS` was pinned to nothing — which is how far the new cell got before anything noticed the mint wrote it and every reader dropped it. Now pinned, field maps included.\n\nBoth MAJORs are mutation-proven (reverting each reds its regression), and `RESYNC_PACK.md` carries the adopter migration — which surfaced that `Supersedes` and `Brief` never got entries either, named there rather than silently fixed."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":332161,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b2631cfa-91b4-4804-b502-44aa0db12b75","uuid":"e691b697-c728-42ca-9a71-97906332965e","request_id":"req_011CeeC2okhmTvz2eQc7Bbyq"}
